WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.730
What’s happening to your tax money?

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.040
President Trump said,

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.630
"I'm going to cut some departments."

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:06.860
We’re proposing a budget

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.520
that will shrink the bloated federal bureaucracy.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.940
But that didn't happen.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.600
Quietly, Congress increased spending

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.060
on the very departments Trump wanted to cut.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.220
Important sounding agencies like

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.960
the Agriculture Department.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.220
Which raises the question.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.300
What does the Agriculture Department do?

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.900
Um I'm sure they do a bunch of things.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.680
No one I asked knew.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.200
What does agriculture do?

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:33.700
FDA?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.480
No.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.680
3/4ths of the money goes for programs

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.100
like food stamps

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.220
And lots of that is wasted.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.080
Billions went to dead people.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.100
And billions more go for corporate welfare,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.360
farm subsidies.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.260
Years ago, politicians said,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.260
government must help farmers

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.300
to make sure America has an ample food supply.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.720
The whole thing is a big boondoggle which

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.700
gives some farmers subsidies,

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.440
but the vast majority of farmers don’t get subsidized

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.119
and it still gets grown.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.480
Yes, somehow, we always have enough vegetables

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.740
and fruit,

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.740
crops that don’t get subsidies.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.460
The subsidies mostly go to grain and corn farmers.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.600
The richest farmers get most of the handouts.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.600
What they’re really doing is taking from
the private sector

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.900
and they’re giving it to special interests.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.140
And yet at the same time, the government demands

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.080
other farmers grow less.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.200
To prop up cherry prices, the department told this farmer,

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.940
“destroy your crop!”

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.280
He had to dump

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.320
40,000 lbs

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.600
of perfectly good cherries

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.100
on the ground and let them rot.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.340
The result is we have fewer cherries

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.740
and we have to pay more for existing cherries.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.880
That’s not helping.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.220
Other cabinet departments are just as wasteful.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.360
What about the Commerce Department?

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.640
What do they do?

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.540
I have no idea.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.000
No one did.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.040
The department’s biggest spending item is

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.920
supporting the global warming science complex.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.720
The ice is also thinning at an alarming rate.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.800
The Commerce Department spends your money

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.260
at an alarming rate.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.120
They bought a $300,000 yacht

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.040
which the bureaucrats used to go fishing.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.820
The department also gives money to

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.720
companies that have tech problems.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.460
They claim: “every dollar generates $30.”

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.040
They take a $1

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.600
and then they get

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.480
$30 of benefits for society.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.140
All we need to do is take more of your dollar

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.860
and we get 30 times the amount.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:33.220
The unseen is, if we’re not spending that $1,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.820
that’s being taken from the economy too.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.080
So if we spend that $1,

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.600
why doesn’t that become $30?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.340
It’s the biggest Ponzi scheme example

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.980
logic I’ve heard of.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.260
And think about just this idea

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.560
of a commerce department.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.140
When one of the founders was asked about

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.240
about creating the department, he said

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.040
"for heaven's sake,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.780
what is meant by a government Chamber of Commerce?”

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.470
Commerce just happens.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.980
We don’t need a Commerce Department.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.540
$14 back, thank you sir.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.080
Why don’t we just let people do what they
want to do

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.300
– interact freely.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.020
Wouldn’t that be nice!

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.640
But that’s not happening,

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:14.100
under Democrats and Republicans, government grows.

